{
  "dom_id": "step-q555452",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Between which two consecutive whole numbers does $\\sqrt{40}$ lie?",
  "worked_solution": "To find which two consecutive whole numbers $\\sqrt{40}$ lies between, we first identify the perfect squares that are just below and just above $40.$\n\nThe perfect squares closest to $40$ are $36$ and $49.$ We have\n\n$$\n36<40<49.\n$$\n\nTaking the square root of each number, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{36} & <\\sqrt{40}<\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 6 & <\\sqrt{40}<7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/5c2775762ff274451dfd3258bacbede7240e6bad25b782cc86a76484e61d31bb.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\sqrt{40}$ lies between $6$ and $7.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
